# A package's manifest as Term holds it: the shape of deck/deck/code/form.ts's `DeckManifest` and of the records it
# carries, written for the port of deck/deck/code/manifest.ts (term-cli-in-term-0074) and read by every port of the
# package lane after it.
#
# The decisions:
#   - the version and every hold are version.tree's `code` and `code-hold`, so a field the TypeScript left out is
#     written as nothing there: `<>` for no prerelease or build, `-1` for a wildcard's open part. code/code.ts is the
#     face that turns those back
#   - an optional text, flag, list or hash is a plain `need false` field (stdlib-parity decision 001): left out of a
#     `make` it reads as its empty value, which is all the writer asks of it, and on TypeScript it stays absent, so a
#     reader that binds it only when the original had it answers the original's object
#   - a link's `have` and the `need` line are `like maybe` with `need false`, because there the writer tells absent
#     from empty: `have 0` is written, a missing `have` is not. So is `hook`, so a read of it writes nothing back
#   - a `like maybe` field with `need false` is stored bare on TypeScript (self-host traps T002), so every field has
#     the TypeScript shape's name and value; `hook` is a Map where the original held an object

load @term/base/maybe
  find maybe

load ../version
  find code
  find code-hold

# `mind <Name>, base <email>, site <url>`, and `cite`, which has the same shape
form deck-mind
  link name, like text
  link base
    like text
    need false
  link site
    like text
    need false

# `link @scope/name, mark <hold>, have <n>`
form deck-link
  link name, like text
  link mark, like code-hold
  link have
    like maybe, like number
    need false

# `host <registry>` with `link` children: dependencies pinned to one registry
form deck-host-group
  link registry, like text
  link link, like list, like deck-link

# `base alice, <ghcr.io/alice-gh/term>`: the scope with its `@`, and where its packages come from
form deck-base
  link scope, like text
  link registry, like text

# `need @term/code, mark <2.6.x>`: the toolchain the project builds with
form deck-need
  link name, like text
  link mark, like code-hold

form deck-manifest
  link host, like text
  link name, like text
  link mark, like code
  link code
    like text
    need false
  link head
    like text
    need false
  link mind
    like list, like deck-mind
    need false
  link lock
    like text
    need false
  link sort
    like text
    need false
  link term
    like list, like text
    need false
  link link, like list, like deck-link
  # a maybe so that reading it writes nothing back: a plain `need false` hash read on TypeScript is `??=`, which would
  # put an empty hash into the manifest it reads (self-host traps T003)
  link hook
    like maybe
      like hash, like text
        like text
    need false
  link role
    like text
    need false
  link test
    like text
    need false
  link book
    like text
    need false
  link line
    like text
    need false
  link call
    like text
    need false
  link task
    like text
    need false
  link hide
    like boolean
    need false
  link site
    like text
    need false
  link view
    like text
    need false
  link deck
    like list, like text
    need false
  link dev-link
    like list, like deck-link
    need false
  link host-link
    like list, like deck-host-group
    need false
  link base
    like list, like deck-base
    need false
  link boot
    like text
    need false
  link tool
    like text
    need false
  link text
    like text
    need false
  link make
    like list, like text
    need false
  link cite
    like list, like deck-mind
    need false
  link need
    like maybe, like deck-need
    need false
